# Frontend Development Rules (Next.js 16 + Tailwind CSS v4)

## Package Manager
- Use `pnpm` (not npm, not yarn)

## Build & Lint
- Build: `pnpm run build`
- Lint: `pnpm run lint`
- Fix all lint errors before claiming work complete

## Styling
- Use Tailwind CSS v4 with `@theme` engine
- All components must be presentation-layer only
- NO direct database connections, NO ORM, NO backend workers

## Components
- Use React 19+ with Radix UI primitives
- All components must be strictly client-side presentation
- No backend logic in frontend code

## API Client
- Use typed OpenAPI client generated from FastAPI's `/openapi.json`
- All API calls must go through the generated client
- No manual fetch calls or direct API access

## Conventions
- No backend logic, ORM, or direct DB connections
- Presentation layer only - styling, components, UI logic
- Follow Tailwind CSS v4 patterns
- Use Radix UI primitives for accessibility